  "slug": "prediction-drug-0697",
  "summary": "Pretrained protein language model embeddings are being read out directly for motifs, local structure, and homology search.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is reuse of pretrained protein language model embeddings as the readout itself rather than as inputs to hand-crafted features. A concept activation vector applied to these embeddings localizes 69 motifs with over 85% F1. Mean-pooling embeddings over sliding windows reveals local structural similarity between proteins from sequence alone. TEA derives a 20-letter protein alphabet via contrastive learning on the same embeddings, enabling fast remote homology search. What is new is the use of embedding geometry: concept vectors for site detection, window pooling for local structural inference, and learned discrete alphabets for sequence comparison. The evidence here consists of three preprints, each summarized at the abstract level.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-30"
}
